1. Define the variables and equations in MATLAB:

```matlab
syms a b c p q r x
eq1 = ap + bq + cr == 28;
eq2 = a + b + c == 10;
eq3 = x == a + 2*b - c/3;
```

2. Solve the system of equations for "a", "b", and "c":

```matlab
sol = solve([eq1, eq2, eq3], [a, b, c]);
```

3. Substitute the values of "a", "b", and "c" from the solution into the equation for "x":

```matlab
x_value = subs(eq3, {a, b, c}, sol);
```

4. Simplify the expression for "x_value":

```matlab
x_value = simplify(x_value);
