```javascript
import { Credentials } from 'react-native-fbsdk';

const credentials = new Credentials({
  appId: 'YOUR_APP_ID', // Replace with your app ID
  accessToken: 'YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN', // Replace with your access token (if needed)
});

export default credentials;
```

Replace `YOUR_APP_ID` with your actual app ID and `YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN` with your access token (if you have one).

3. In your component where you want to use the credentials, import the `Credentials` object and use it like this:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { View, Text } from 'react-native';
import { Credentials } from './Credentials';

const MyComponent = () => {
  const { appId, accessToken } = Credentials;

  return (
    <View>
      <Text>App ID: {appId}</Text>
      <Text>Access Token: {accessToken}</Text>
    </View>
  );
};

export default MyComponent;
```

Now, you have passed the credentials in your JavaScript code for `react-native-fbsdk-next`. You can use these credentials to authenticate users, make API calls, or perform other actions related to your Facebook app.

