3. You will see a list of available widget areas and the widgets currently assigned to them.
4. To rearrange the layout of the widgets, click and drag the widgets to the desired position.
5. You can also add new widgets by clicking on the "Add a Widget" button and selecting the widget you want to add from the list.
6. Once you have made your changes, click on the "Publish" button to save your changes.

Method 2: Adding custom CSS

1. Log in to your WordPress dashboard and go to "Appearance" > "Editor".
2. Select the "Theme Files" option from the dropdown menu.
3. Find the file called "style.css" (or a similar file) and click on it to open it.
4. Add the following CSS code at the bottom of the file:
```css
/* Custom widget layout */
.widget-area {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;
  justify-content: space-between;
}

.widget {
  width: calc(33.33% - 10px);
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}
```
This code will create a flexible grid layout for your widgets, with each widget taking up one-third of the available space. You can adjust the `width` and `margin-bottom` values to customize the layout further.

5. Save the file and refresh your WordPress dashboard to see the changes.

Remember to replace the example CSS code with your own custom CSS if you want to achieve a different layout.

